<title>USA: USDA Dec 12 world grain highlights.</title>
<headline>USDA Dec 12 world grain highlights.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>World grain crops will total 1,841.78 million tonnes in 1996/97, the U.S. Agriculture Department said Thursday, compared to last month's estimate of 1.841.31 million tonnes and last year's 1,703.25 million. Wheat was pegged at 579.59 million tonnes, coarse grains at 885.42 million and rice at 376.77 million. Oilseeds were forecast at 255.28 million tonnes and cotton at 85.93 million bales.</p>
<p>The European Union was forecast to import 14.37 million tonnes of soybeans and 16.12 million of soymeal. China's imports were pegged at 6.0 million tonnes of wheat, 1.5 million of soybeans and 1.8 million of soybean meal.  </p>
